j=A.ar(["prosperity","PREPARATION: Set your journal and pen on a stable surface. Fill a small bowl with clean water to represent the Nile. Place a coin, budget, or written financial goal beside it if available. Otherwise, write down one resource you already have.","love","PREPARATION: Set out your journal and pen. Place two flowers or small objects side by side to symbolize mutual care, or write two qualities you value in a healthy relationship.","protection","PREPARATION: Gather clean water and a clean cloth. Wipe a small surface, wash or gently wipe your hands, and dry them before writing. This symbolic cleansing does not replace practical safety measures.","lunar","PREPARATION: Set out your journal and pen. Observe the Moon if visible, consult a lunar calendar, or write about a change occurring in your life. Outdoor observation is not required.","dreams","PREPARATION: Open your journal to a fresh page and write the date. Record a remembered dream and its emotions. If you remember no dream, write a recent thought or concern instead.","ancestors","PREPARATION: Place a photograph or keepsake nearby, write the name of someone you wish to remember, or recall a meaningful story. Keep your journal ready to record one memory or lesson."],k,k)
i=A.ar(["prosperity","SPOKEN INVOCATION (modern composition): As the Nile nourished the land, may wisdom guide how I care for what I have. May I pursue prosperity without harming others, practice fairness in every exchange, and build stability through patient and responsible work. Let gratitude shape my choices and let my actions support a sustainable future.","love","SPOKEN INVOCATION (modern composition): May kindness guide my words and respect guide my actions. May I give care freely without seeking control, welcome affection without abandoning my boundaries, and recognize the dignity of every person. Let honesty, patience, and reciprocity strengthen the relationships I choose to nurture.","protection","SPOKEN INVOCATION (modern composition): May clarity steady my thoughts and courage support my decisions. May I recognize danger without surrendering to fear, honor my boundaries, and take wise steps toward safety. Let my words reflect truth, my actions reflect balance, and my choices protect the well-being of myself and others.","lunar","SPOKEN INVOCATION (modern composition): As the Moon moves through its changing phases, may I recognize the seasons of my own life. May I meet beginnings with purpose, uncertainty with patience, and endings with understanding. Let my intentions become practical actions and my reflections lead to meaningful growth.","dreams","SPOKEN INVOCATION (modern composition): May I approach the images of sleep with curiosity and discernment. Let me remember what I truly experienced, distinguish possibility from certainty, and seek wisdom without confusing symbols with proof. May reflection deepen my self-understanding and guide thoughtful choices in waking life.","ancestors","SPOKEN INVOCATION (modern composition): I remember those whose lives and teachings helped shape my path. May I honor their humanity, preserve what was wise, and learn from what was difficult. Let remembrance become compassion, gratitude become service, and the lessons of the past guide responsible action today."],k,k)
h=A.ar(["prosperity","CEREMONIAL CLOSING: Look at the bowl of water and acknowledge the resources supporting your life. Say: May gratitude accompany what I receive, fairness guide what I exchange, and wisdom guide what I preserve. Record your next financial action. Pour away the water respectfully and put the bowl away.","love","CEREMONIAL CLOSING: Look at your flowers, objects, or written qualities. Say: May my relationships be rooted in dignity, freely chosen affection, honesty, and mutual care. Record one act of kindness that respects your boundaries. Put your materials away.","protection","CEREMONIAL CLOSING: Place your clean cloth beside the water. Say: May clear judgment guide my steps, healthy boundaries protect my peace, and responsible action strengthen my safety. Record one practical protective measure. Put away your materials and leave the space clean.","lunar","CEREMONIAL CLOSING: Reflect on the Moon or the life transition you recorded. Say: I honor the changes behind me, the responsibilities before me, and the possibilities still unfolding. Write one next step and close your journal.","dreams","CEREMONIAL CLOSING: Read your dream notes without judgment. Say: I welcome insight with curiosity, examine meaning with care, and remain grounded in what I can know. Underline one useful reflection and close your notebook.","ancestors","CEREMONIAL CLOSING: Look at your keepsake or remembered name. Say: I carry forward what was wise, learn from what was difficult, and honor memory through compassionate action. Record one lesson to preserve and return your keepsake to its place if used."],k,k)
g=A.ar(["prosperity","WEEKLY OBSERVANCE: Review seven days of spending, saving, giving, and obligations. Record one decision that supported stability and one that needs improvement. Choose a realistic financial action for the coming week.","love","WEEKLY OBSERVANCE: Reflect on how you offered and received care this week. Record one moment of healthy communication and one boundary worth strengthening. Choose a respectful act of appreciation.","protection","WEEKLY OBSERVANCE: Review your personal safety, privacy, and boundaries. Identify one precaution that worked and one vulnerability you can address. Write a practical safety action for the next seven days.","lunar","WEEKLY OBSERVANCE: Review how your intention developed during the past seven days. Note what changed, what remains unfinished, and one adjustment that better aligns your actions with your goals.","dreams","WEEKLY OBSERVANCE: Review your dream journal or reflection notes from the past week. Identify recurring emotions or themes without treating them as predictions. Write one question for further reflection.","ancestors","WEEKLY OBSERVANCE: Recall a family story, teaching, or memory. Write down one detail worth preserving and one constructive way to honor that lesson during the coming week."],k,k)
