B.OK=s(["DAILY AFFIRMATIONS\n\nBegin in a quiet place. Take three slow breaths. Speak each affirmation three times, allowing its meaning to settle in your heart.\n\nGRATITUDE\nCreator of the Universe, I give thanks for the life I have, the lessons I receive, and the opportunities before me.\n\nPROSPERITY\nI welcome honorable prosperity. I use wisdom, discipline, and gratitude to care for what I receive.\n\nLOVE\nI welcome relationships grounded in kindness, honesty, mutual respect, and peace.\n\nPROTECTION\nI move with awareness, courage, and healthy boundaries. I choose peace without surrendering my strength.\n\nWISDOM\nI listen carefully, learn continually, and act with clear judgment.\n\nRENEWAL\nToday I release what no longer serves my growth and make room for a better beginning.\n\nREFLECTION\nWrite one affirmation in your journal. Record one practical action you can take today.\n\nCLOSING\nBringing harm to none as it comes.\nThis I accept, so mote it be.","MOON PHASES\n\nThe Moon's phases are changes in how much of its sunlit half we can see from Earth. A complete cycle lasts approximately 29.5 days. The following spiritual associations are reflective traditions, not scientific predictions.\n\nNEW MOON \u2014 BEGINNINGS\nChoose a clear intention. Write your sacred letter at home in a peaceful environment. Reflect on the first practical step you can take. The new moon is generally not visible.\n\nWAXING CRESCENT \u2014 COMMITMENT\nReview your intention and take one small, deliberate step toward it.\n\nFIRST QUARTER \u2014 ACTION\nConsider an obstacle and choose a constructive response.\n\nWAXING GIBBOUS \u2014 REFINEMENT\nImprove your plan. Practice patience and consistency.\n\nFULL MOON \u2014 GRATITUDE AND RELEASE\nReflect on what has grown. Express thanks to the Creator of the Universe and consider what you are ready to release.\n\nWANING GIBBOUS \u2014 SHARING\nOffer gratitude, share what you have learned, and support others when appropriate.\n\nLAST QUARTER \u2014 REASSESSMENT\nLet go of an unhelpful habit or expectation.\n\nWANING CRESCENT \u2014 REST\nRest, journal, and prepare for the next cycle.\n\nRITUAL NOTE\nYour sacred letter is prepared at home. Outdoors, focus on your intention, recite the written words three times, and meditate. Follow the four-directions release instructions in your chosen ritual. Never burn paper inside a closed Mason jar; heat can shatter glass. Where outdoor fires are not permitted, use a fire-free symbolic release.","MEDITATIONS\n\n20-MINUTE CONNECTION PRACTICE\n\nMINUTES 0\u20133 \u2014 ARRIVE\nChoose a lawful, quiet, accessible outdoor location. Stand or sit comfortably. Feel the ground supporting you and notice the air around you.\n\nMINUTES 3\u20136 \u2014 BREATHE\nBreathe gently and naturally. Relax your shoulders and unclench your jaw. There is no need to force or hold your breath.\n\nMINUTES 6\u20139 \u2014 GRATITUDE\nSilently thank the Creator of the Universe for life, lessons, and opportunities. Honor Ra as a symbol of sunlight and Thoth as a symbol of lunar wisdom and sacred writing.\n\nMINUTES 9\u201313 \u2014 SACRED WORDS\nHold the letter you prepared at home. Read your complete written intention aloud three times, slowly and with attention. Memorizing the words is optional; sincerity and focus matter more than perfect recall.\n\nMINUTES 13\u201317 \u2014 STILLNESS\nRest in silence. Return your attention to your breathing whenever your thoughts wander. Notice your feelings without forcing a particular sensation.\n\nMINUTES 17\u201320 \u2014 REFLECTION\nConsider one action that aligns with your intention. Complete the release and closing instructions in the selected ritual when safe and appropriate.\n\nGROUNDING OPTION\nIf you feel overwhelmed, open your eyes, notice five things around you, and return to ordinary breathing. You may end the practice at any time.","SPIRITUAL TOOLS\n\nCORE MATERIALS\nBlack Sharpie, paper for the complete sacred letter, and a Mason jar for carrying or storing the letter. Prepare and write the full letter at home in a peaceful environment. No table or elaborate altar is required.\n\nFIRE SAFETY\nA Mason jar is not a fireproof burning vessel. Never ignite paper inside a sealed or ordinary glass jar; it can crack or shatter. If burning is legal and safe, use an appropriate outdoor fireproof metal vessel, keep water nearby, and extinguish completely. Never scatter hot embers or ashes into the wind. A fire-free alternative is to tear the letter into four pieces and symbolically acknowledge the four directions, then dispose of the paper responsibly.\n\nTWELVE SACRED STONES\nThese are symbolic spiritual associations, not scientifically established effects.\n\n1. Jade \u2014 Prosperity, abundance, harmony, financial wisdom. Recommended for Prosperity.\n2. Tiger's Eye \u2014 Courage, confidence, grounding. Recommended for Protection.\n3. Amethyst \u2014 Calm, reflection, intuition. Recommended for Protection and Dreams.\n4. Rose Quartz \u2014 Compassion, emotional harmony, self-love. Recommended for Love.\n5. Moonstone \u2014 Lunar cycles, renewal, intuition. Recommended for Moon and Manifestation.\n6. Black Onyx \u2014 Resilience, grounding, remembrance. Recommended for Ancestors.\n7. Citrine \u2014 Optimism, creativity, opportunity. Recommended for Prosperity.\n8. Clear Quartz \u2014 Clarity, focus, intentionality.\n9. Lapis Lazuli \u2014 Wisdom, truth, communication.\n10. Labradorite \u2014 Reflection, change, imagination.\n11. Carnelian \u2014 Motivation, courage, creativity.\n12. Obsidian \u2014 Grounding, self-examination, boundaries.\n\nStones and spiritual jewelry are optional. Your attention, written words, and personal intention remain central.","ARTICLES & LESSONS\n\nLESSON 1 \u2014 THE CREATOR AND THE UNIVERSE\nJustice Divine invites reflection on the Creator of the Universe, gratitude for life, and responsible action. Spiritual interpretations are personal and need not be presented as scientific facts.\n\nLESSON 2 \u2014 RA AND THOTH\nRa is an ancient Egyptian solar deity. Thoth is associated with writing, wisdom, and the Moon. Their symbols can inform a modern reflective practice. The Justice Divine letters are original, Egyptian-inspired ceremonies, not verified reproductions of ancient rites.\n\nLESSON 3 \u2014 WRITING YOUR SACRED LETTER\nAt home, find a quiet place. Use a black Sharpie and paper to write the entire letter you intend to recite: your gratitude, intention, requests for wisdom and good energy, commitments to action, and closing words. Read it over before leaving. Bring the completed letter to your chosen outdoor location.\n\nLESSON 4 \u2014 THREE RECITATIONS\nUnder the open sky, center your attention. Recite everything written in the letter three times, with deliberate pauses. You may memorize the letter, but reading it is equally acceptable. Meditate until you feel settled; a particular physical sensation is not required.\n\nLESSON 5 \u2014 THE FOUR DIRECTIONS\nFace North for grounding, West for reflection, South for courage, and East for new light. Speak a short intention toward each direction. Release the letter symbolically and responsibly. If using fire, obey local restrictions, use a suitable fireproof container, fully extinguish ashes, and do not scatter them into the wind. A fire-free release is always acceptable.\n\nLESSON 6 \u2014 RESPONSIBLE STEWARDSHIP\nPair spiritual intentions with real-world steps: care for relationships, protect your well-being, manage resources wisely, and act with integrity.\n\nUNIVERSAL CLOSING\nBringing harm to none as it comes.\nThis I accept, so mote it be.","VOICE GUIDANCE \u2014 READ-ALOUD SCRIPTS\n\nThese scripts are ready for spoken delivery. Audio playback is not enabled in this version of the Guidance tab.\n\nOPENING \u2014 ABOUT 30 SECONDS\nWelcome to Justice Divine. Find a quiet, comfortable place. Breathe gently. Notice the ground beneath you and the space around you. Bring your attention to gratitude, wisdom, and the intention you have chosen today.\n\nGRATITUDE \u2014 ABOUT 30 SECONDS\nCreator of the Universe, thank you for this moment, for the opportunity to learn, and for the strength to move forward with compassion. I welcome good energy and commit to honorable action.\n\nFOCUS \u2014 ABOUT 45 SECONDS\nAs you breathe, allow distractions to pass. Return to your words. If you have prepared a sacred letter, recite it slowly three times. After each reading, pause and consider what the words mean to you.\n\nCLOSING \u2014 ABOUT 20 SECONDS\nMay I move forward with clarity, gratitude, and peace. Bringing harm to none as it comes. This I accept, so mote it be.\n\nNOTE\nFor now, read these scripts aloud yourself. Actual play, pause, and spoken-audio controls will require a separate text-to-speech implementation."],t.s)
